---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const skills = [
  ['Statistics & ML', 'regression, mixed models, gradient boosting, uncertainty quantification'],
  ['Spatial analysis', 'point patterns, kriging, hex binning, network and raster analysis'],
  ['Data engineering', 'Python, SQL, PostGIS, DuckDB, reproducible pipelines'],
  ['Visualisation', 'static SVG, MapLibre/Leaflet, Observable Plot, D3'],
];
---
<Base title="About" description="About Lucis Labs.">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">about</p><h1>About</h1></div>
    <p>Lucis Labs is a one-person research practice working at the seam between data science and geography. Most useful questions have a "where" attached, and most spatial datasets are too small or too autocorrelated for naive statistics.</p>
    <h2>Toolkit</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      {skills.map(([t, d]) => (<div class="card"><h3 style="margin:0 0 6px">{t}</h3><p class="mute" style="margin:0">{d}</p></div>))}
    </div>
    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>Built with Astro. Charts are SVG rendered at build time with D3 modules. The atlas data is generated by <code>src/lib/geo.ts</code> and served as static GeoJSON. Every push to <code>main</code> deploys through GitHub Actions to GitHub Pages.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
